	<item>
		<title>By: Patrice Villastrgio</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=695&#038;cpage=1#comment-48743</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Patrice Villastrgio]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 27 Jan 2015 18:22:57 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=695#comment-48743</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[I too remember Sarmad from the Greenwood Natural Food Store and Restaurant in San Antonio, Texas. I just had to be part of the energy at that place! So, I lied about my age and started working there, cooking, until I nearly cut off my thumb.  My age was discovered at the hospital, but by then I was 16. Sarmad allowed me to stay, moving me and my wrapped hand to the front as cashier.  Amazing, and patient, man!
Sarmad was a kind and gentle soul, the voice of home to all who heard it, the inspiration of peace to those who needed it, and offered love with every breath.  He was a darn good business man, too!
Love to the family...and all who knew this wonderful man.
His light will forever shine with ours * &gt;*
Love on...
Patrice]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I too remember Sarmad from the Greenwood Natural Food Store and Restaurant in San Antonio, Texas. I just had to be part of the energy at that place! So, I lied about my age and started working there, cooking, until I nearly cut off my thumb.  My age was discovered at the hospital, but by then I was 16. Sarmad allowed me to stay, moving me and my wrapped hand to the front as cashier.  Amazing, and patient, man!<br />
Sarmad was a kind and gentle soul, the voice of home to all who heard it, the inspiration of peace to those who needed it, and offered love with every breath.  He was a darn good business man, too!<br />
Love to the family&#8230;and all who knew this wonderful man.<br />
His light will forever shine with ours * &gt;*<br />
Love on&#8230;<br />
Patrice</p>
]]></content:encoded>
